<h1>Warden Lite Privacy Policy</h1>
 
<p>Effective Date: October 26, 2026</p>
 
<p>
This policy explains what information Warden Lite, a Discord moderation, logging and security bot, collects,
how it is used, and how to ask for it to be deleted.
</p>
 
<h2>1. Information Warden Lite Stores</h2>
<p>Warden Lite keeps a separate database for each server it is in. Depending on which features a server uses, it may store:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Discord IDs and names:</strong> user, server, channel and role IDs, and usernames, so actions can be linked to the right accounts.</li>
<li><strong>Moderation cases:</strong> warnings, mutes, timeouts, kicks and bans, including the member, the staff member or automatic system that acted, the reason, any evidence or notes staff added, durations, and whether a notice DM was delivered.</li>
<li><strong>Verification records</strong> (if enabled): join time, verification deadline, number of attempts, status and how verification was completed. CAPTCHA answers are stored only as a one-way hash.</li>
<li><strong>Join information:</strong> account age at the time of joining, used for raid detection and the optional account-age gate.</li>
<li><strong>Anti-spam data:</strong> a simplified fingerprint of recent message text and any links in it, used to detect repeated spam. These records are deleted after 24 hours.</li>
<li><strong>Security events:</strong> records of server changes such as channel, role, ban and permission changes, and who made them, used to detect nukes and raids.</li>
<li><strong>AFK status:</strong> the AFK reason a member sets with <code>/afk</code>, until it is cleared.</li>
<li><strong>Blocklist:</strong> if the developer blocks a server or a server owner from using Warden Lite, it stores the server ID and name, the owner's user ID, the reason, and when the block was made, so it can leave if it's added again.</li>
<li><strong>Server settings:</strong> staff roles, channels, feature settings and any custom text a server writes (for example welcome messages and rules).</li>
</ul>
 
<h2>2. Information Warden Lite Does Not Store</h2>
<ul>
<li>Warden Lite does <strong>not</strong> keep a copy of members' messages in its database. When a message is edited or deleted, the server's own <code>#message-logs</code> channel receives the log, and it stays there under that server's control.</li>
<li>Images and videos checked by the optional media scanner are processed temporarily and deleted straight after the check. They are not saved.</li>
<li>Warden Lite does not collect passwords, payment details, or information from outside Discord.</li>
</ul>
 
<h2>3. How Information Is Used</h2>
<p>
Information is used only to run Warden Lite's features in the server it came from: moderation, case history, logging,
verification, anti-spam, the link filter, warning escalation, security monitoring and lockdowns.
Logs and cases are posted into that server's own Warden Lite channels, which only that server's staff can see.
Information is never sold, rented or used for advertising, and one server's data is not shown to other servers.
</p>
 
<h2>4. Services Warden Lite Uses</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Discord:</strong> Warden Lite runs through the Discord API, and Discord's own <a href="https://discord.com/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> applies to your use of Discord.</li>
<li><strong>Scam-link list:</strong> the optional link filter downloads a public list of known scam domains. No user information is sent when it does this.</li>
</ul>
 
<h2>5. Storage and Retention</h2>
<p>
Data is stored on the developer's own computer, in a database for each server, with daily backups that are kept for 21 days.
Anti-spam records are deleted after 24 hours. Other records, such as moderation cases, are kept so staff can see a member's history
until the server's data is deleted. If Warden Lite is removed from a server, that server's data is kept until deletion is requested.
</p>
 
<h2>6. Deleting Your Data</h2>
<p>
Server owners can ask for all of their server's Warden Lite data to be deleted. Members can ask for their own records to be deleted.
Some records, such as active moderation cases, may be kept where they are needed to keep a server safe, and the server's staff will be told about the request.
Send requests to the developer in the Spawn of the Pack Discord server.
</p>
 
<h2>7. Children</h2>
<p>
Warden Lite is intended for use on Discord, which requires users to meet Discord's minimum age.
It does not knowingly collect information beyond what is described above.
</p>
 
<h2>8. Changes to This Policy</h2>
<p>
This policy may be updated as Warden Lite changes. The effective date above shows when it last changed.
</p>
 
<h2>9. Contact</h2>
<p>
For privacy questions or data deletion requests, contact the developer in the Spawn of the Pack Discord server:
<a href="https://discord.gg/smXWcBbEjJ">discord.gg/smXWcBbEjJ</a>
</p>
 
